# SABOTAGE: T160 (spec §I4 completion) — a set-but-BROKEN `billing_customer_id` anchor
# (wrong org, or pointing at a deleted/nonexistent customer) now silently FALLS THROUGH
# to `domain_match/2` instead of resolving to honest absence. The anchor is documented
# as AUTHORITATIVE — "the fallback below is NEVER consulted, even if it would resolve to
# a DIFFERENT customer" — precisely because a stale/corrupt anchor pointing at the WRONG
# org must never be silently "fixed" by re-guessing via domain (that re-guess could land
# on a genuinely different, wrong customer, and worse, masks the data-integrity bug the
# broken anchor represents). This mutation makes a broken anchor behave AS IF it were
# unset, defeating the authoritative guarantee. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: samen_web
# TEST_FILES: test/samen/web/crm_account_health_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: T160 ANCHOR-AUTHORITATIVE, but BROKEN (wrong org / deleted) -> honest absence, NEVER a silent re-guess via domain
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/crm/account_link.ex
@@ -110,8 +110,14 @@
   @spec resolve(struct(), Config.t()) :: {:ok, struct(), :anchor | :domain} | {:error, :not_linked}
   def resolve(company, %Config{} = config) do
     case anchor_id(company) do
-      nil -> domain_match(company, config)
-      id -> anchor_match(id, config)
